course: dictionary
lesson: 2776
title: Words that show how bad something is
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: «Disgracefully» is an adverb. It tells you how someone did something, and in this sense it means in a way that is shameful and very bad. When you read it, ask: did someone do something so bad that they should feel ashamed?
explain: «Toad came down to breakfast disgracefully late.» Toad was not just a little late. The word disgracefully tells you he was late in a way that people would scold him for. Read the words around it, and the story tells you the same thing: the breakfast was cold and mostly gone.
explain: Disgracefully has a second meaning too, which adds a strong feeling of "far too much". «The room was disgracefully dirty» means it was shockingly dirty, far worse than it should be. Swap in "shamefully" or "shockingly" to check: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Disgracefully means in a way that is shameful and very bad.
fact: «Disgracefully» is an adverb, so it tells you how something was done, such as «behave disgracefully».
fact: As an intensifier, disgracefully means shockingly, or far too much: «disgracefully late» means much too late.
fact: «Disgracefully» is often used by grown-ups when they are telling someone off.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad is told more than once that he has behaved disgracefully.
exercise: «Toad came down to breakfast disgracefully late.» What does disgracefully mean here? | Happily early | Slightly tired | *Shamefully late, in a way people would scold | Quietly, with no noise
exercise: Someone says, «You have behaved disgracefully!» What are they doing? | *Telling you off, saying what you did was shameful | Singing a song | Giving you a prize | Asking for directions
exercise: Nadia says disgracefully only ever means rude. Is she right? | Yes, it always means rude and nothing else | *No, it can also mean shockingly poor or far too much, as in «disgracefully dirty» | It is the name of a place | It means very happy
test: «The room was disgracefully dirty.» What does disgracefully tell you about dirty? | It is wet | It is a little bit dirty | It is clean and shiny | *It is shockingly, far too dirty
test: Which sentence shows someone behaving disgracefully? | *He ate his friend's sandwich and then lied about it | He read a book quietly | He said sorry and helped tidy up | He shared his toys with his little sister
exam: Toad came down to breakfast «disgracefully late». Which word is the adverb that tells you how late? | Toad | *disgracefully | breakfast | late
